> If FSR2.2 is a valid TAA option then we need to do more to communicate to the user that it shouldn't be used with TAA. Right now you can enable FSR2.2 and TAA at the same time. But it clearly just uses FSR2.2

I forgot to mention the current approach shows a warning on the console similar to the rest of the behavior when upscalers are used with invalid configurations. Do you think we need something better?

This is the current handling:
```cpp
if (use_taa && scaling_3d_mode == RS::VIEWPORT_SCALING_3D_MODE_FSR2) {
	// FSR2 can't be used with TAA.
	// Turn it off and prefer using FSR2.
	WARN_PRINT_ONCE("FSR 2 is not compatible with TAA. Turning TAA off.");
	use_taa = false;
}
```
